meta {
  name: Renewal Outreach Desk
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/crm/service-tickets/renewals/desk
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{crmAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns an array of desk rows", function () {
    expect(res.getBody()).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("every row carries the fields the desk renders", function () {
    for (const row of res.getBody()) {
      expect(row).to.have.property("cycleId");
      expect(row).to.have.property("ticketId");
      expect(row).to.have.property("stepKey");
      expect(row).to.have.property("label");
      expect(row).to.have.property("clientName");
      expect(row).to.have.property("renewalDate");
      expect(row).to.have.property("daysUntilRenewal");
      expect(row).to.have.property("daysUntilAvailable");
      expect(row).to.have.property("assignedUserId");
      expect(row).to.have.property("assignedRep");
      expect(row.policies).to.be.an("array");
    }
  });

  test("every row is a call that has not opened, inside the preview window", function () {
    // PAC-143: an open call is in the ticket queue, never on the desk.
    for (const row of res.getBody()) {
      expect(row.daysUntilAvailable).to.be.a("number");
      expect(row.daysUntilAvailable).to.be.within(0, 14);
      expect(row.isActionable).to.equal(false);
      expect(row.isOverdue).to.equal(false);
    }
  });

  test("counts down by when each call opens", function () {
    const opens = res.getBody().map((row) => row.daysUntilAvailable);
    expect(opens).to.deep.equal(opens.slice().sort((a, b) => a - b));
  });

  test("one row per cycle", function () {
    const ids = res.getBody().map((row) => row.cycleId);
    expect(new Set(ids).size).to.equal(ids.length);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /crm/service-tickets/renewals/desk

  The **Proactive Renewal Outreach** desk on the Service Dashboard
  (`/crm/service`): renewals whose renewal period is about to start — one row
  per cycle, for the `RENEWAL_DESK_PREVIEW_DAYS` (**14**) days before its
  **first** call opens.

  - **Module:** `crm_service`
  - **Permission:** `crm_service:read`
  - **Data scope (PAC-146):** follows the caller's. An agency-scoped owner sees
    the agency's renewals, a branch-scoped manager their branch's. An
    `own`-scoped CSR is pinned to the calls assigned to them — *not* the branch
    floor the ticket list gives them, because the desk is "my renewals".

  A pure read. Cycles and their call tickets are created by the worker's
  renewal scan (PAC-99), which looks `90 + 14` days ahead so an annual cycle
  exists before its T-90 review can be previewed.

  ## Which renewals (PAC-143)

  A cycle is on the desk from T-104 to T-90 on the annual track and from T-59
  to T-45 on auto, and **leaves it the moment its first call opens**. From then
  on the renewal is work in hand and lives in the ticket queue (Agency Priority
  Tickets), so no renewal is ever listed in both.

  "First call" is `renewal.sequence === 1` — position in the track's full
  plan. A cycle whose T-90 review was suppressed at the cutover holds only its
  T-45 call (`sequence: 2`); its renewal period has already started, so it is
  not previewed even though that call has not opened.

  ## Params

  None.

  ## Response

  `RenewalDeskRow[]` — see `@sfa/shared` `service/renewal.ts`. Sorted soonest
  to open first, then soonest renewal. Capped at 100 rows.

  | field | value on every row |
  |---|---|
  | `daysUntilAvailable` | whole days until the call opens (`0` = later today) — never null |
  | `isActionable` | `false` — `POST …/renewals/steps/:stepKey/complete` refuses a step before its `availableAt` |
  | `isOverdue` | `false` |
  | `assignedUserId` / `assignedRep` | whose call it is — an owner or manager sees other people's |

  Computed against the **server clock**; a browser must not re-derive them from
  `availableAt`.

  ### What is deliberately absent

  No premium-change field. `Policy.premium` is a single current number and the
  system holds no premium history, so an increase cannot be computed; the desk
  shows the renewal window and the call, nothing invented.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | `crm_service` disabled for the agency, or the caller lacks `crm_service:read` |
}
